In the methodology, the Dordrecht address-linked survey data stay inside the ZUT Secure Research Environment. Partners deliver their model outputs (depth grids, ensemble members) to ZUT. The linkage and household-level regression run inside the SRE. Partners receive only disclosure-checked aggregates with at least 10 households per cell. Several cross-town designs are compliant, for example:
- a pooled model fitted inside the SRE;
- a comparison or meta-analysis of town-level estimates;
- an analysis of aggregated block-level indicators.

Partner staff working inside the SRE is also acceptable if no row-level data leave it. The proposal does not describe sending row-level household data or geolocations to WEIH, FBMI or partner laptops. It ties these safeguards to the call's re-identification requirement for maps, datasets and outputs.

